{"w":2400,"lines":[{"w":0.059670778910319022,"c":1,"h":0.016022612545880555,"t":"Test 1","x":0.12757201785332417,"y":0.10029069749999497},{"y":0.13808139499640215,"x":0.45679012297327293,"t":"READING","w":0.12962963104248049,"h":0.020348837575025147,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.12946864945827524,"w":0.2925428009033203,"y":0.19858674092405182,"h":0.019934657605713779},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","x":0.12952104736863959,"w":0.7677753194173178,"h":0.023911897369492618,"c":1,"y":0.2321034974824987},{"t":"Passage 1 below.","y":0.25145348874577023,"w":0.16255143483479814,"h":0.018895348053517669,"x":0.129629632232411,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.29210836235172755,"h":0.02475210241490744,"x":0.34156378931967302,"w":0.36625513712565105,"t":"Nutmeg - a valuable spice"},{"w":0.76768010457356772,"h":0.021664658760996436,"c":1,"x":0.12954067547914766,"y":0.32953599843649661,"t":"The nutmeg tree, Myristica fragrans, is a large evergreen tree native to Southeast Asia. Until the late"},{"h":0.020197019138942895,"t":"18th century, it only grew in one place in the world: a small group of islands in the Banda Sea, part","x":0.1295333431864745,"y":0.34692959657961153,"w":0.76155619303385425,"c":1},{"x":0.12948686102381904,"w":0.74307810465494795,"t":"of the Moluccas - or Spice Islands - in northeastern Indonesia. The tree is thickly branched with","h":0.020187628423648074,"y":0.36322032518635783,"c":1},{"y":0.3801780898504441,"x":0.12950818779287204,"c":1,"t":"dense foliage of tough, dark green oval leaves, and produces small, yellow, bell-shaped flowers and","h":0.020802671973921605,"w":0.75955739339192707},{"y":0.39654904926449552,"h":0.021966657874440965,"c":1,"t":"pale yellow pear-shaped fruits. The fruit is encased in a fleshy husk. When the fruit is ripe, this husk","x":0.12945160927095078,"w":0.76784149169921878},{"w":0.78415191650390637,"c":1,"t":"splits into two halves along a ridge running the length of the fruit. Inside is a purple-brown shiny seed,","y":0.41328127452977537,"h":0.020094558122722428,"x":0.12951346042228834},{"t":"2-3 cm long by about 2 cm across, surrounded by a lacy red or crimson covering called an 'aril'. These","w":0.78843495686848941,"x":0.12945774918937797,"y":0.42796167879694869,"c":1,"h":0.023480409727781759},{"y":0.44613783573451993,"w":0.75762191772460941,"h":0.023629448017888799,"x":0.12946835168254267,"t":"are the sources of the two spices nutmeg and mace, the former being produced from the dried seed","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.12962962930062663,"t":"and the latter from the aril.","y":0.46790341567134963,"w":0.20987654368082684,"h":0.013250883392226132},{"c":1,"w":0.76359980265299487,"h":0.020700574904083502,"y":0.4968855566938698,"t":"Nutmeg was a highly prized and costly ingredient in European cuisine in the Middle Ages, and was","x":0.13157430320044294},{"h":0.020711775241667563,"t":"used as a flavouring, medicinal, and preservative agent. Throughout this period, the Arabs were the","x":0.13154860342401084,"y":0.51354409135712931,"c":1,"w":0.75747716267903653},{"c":1,"t":"exclusive importers of the spice to Europe. They sold nutmeg for high prices to merchants based in","y":0.53014725984677991,"w":0.75953791300455731,"x":0.13155226112521964,"h":0.020428186872682219},{"h":0.020915147132109735,"t":"Venice, but they never revealed the exact location of the source of this extremely valuable commodity.","x":0.13156527087760045,"y":0.54632292949850336,"w":0.78215708414713547,"c":1},{"x":0.1316041963854849,"c":1,"h":0.021096221690183548,"w":0.75740692138671872,"y":0.56379395901990992,"t":"The Arab-Venetian dominance of the trade finally ended in 1512, when the Portuguese reached the"},{"w":0.44855967203776037,"y":0.58274440520902615,"h":0.016195524146054074,"t":"Banda Islands and began exploiting its precious resources.","c":1,"x":0.13374485550508097},{"h":0.023669647243755865,"x":0.13355925298240665,"y":0.61167974676390302,"w":0.74111094156901036,"t":"Always in danger of competition from neighbouring Spain, the Portuguese began subcontracting","c":1},{"w":0.74924123128255204,"h":0.021422892773811375,"t":"their spice distribution to Dutch traders. Profits began to flow into the Netherlands, and the Dutch","y":0.62916535927454409,"x":0.13156496030190984,"c":1},{"y":0.64630593248080026,"w":0.76363464355468758,"t":"commercial fleet swiftly grew into one of the largest in the world. The Dutch quietly gained control","x":0.13155982973937588,"h":0.020415709352886502,"c":1},{"t":"of most of the shipping and trading of spices in Northern Europe. Then, in 1580, Portugal fell under","x":0.13360463747241758,"y":0.66308375598142877,"c":1,"h":0.020862444550746706,"w":0.76778203328450523},{"y":0.67952636331391048,"w":0.78423314412434897,"h":0.021734682494254476,"c":1,"x":0.13359400666586282,"t":"Spanish rule, and by the end of the 16th century the Dutch found themselves locked out of the market."},{"x":0.13361923934919237,"w":0.73685078938802084,"c":1,"t":"As prices for pepper, nutmeg, and other spices soared across Europe, they decided to fight back.","h":0.021275507968502638,"y":0.69675870660105166},{"h":0.021085900889689868,"t":"In 1602, Dutch merchants founded the VOC, a trading corporation better known as the Dutch East","x":0.13361816063971579,"y":0.72965140539335693,"w":0.75746276855468753,"c":1},{"w":0.77202082316080722,"x":0.13353633338850274,"t":"India Company. By 1617, the VOC was the richest commercial operation in the world. The company","h":0.025116705922552551,"c":1,"y":0.74394918889839334},{"y":0.76385551574605814,"w":0.74508661905924489,"h":0.02068399287786582,"t":"had 50,000 employees worldwide, with a private army of 30,000 men and a fleet of 200 ships. At","c":1,"x":0.13364350051919188},{"y":0.7792648519857297,"x":0.13357517594686083,"t":"the same time, thousands of people across Europe were dying of the plague, a highly contagious and","h":0.022955232851637253,"c":1,"w":0.77198796590169272},{"c":1,"t":"deadly disease. Doctors were desperate for a way to stop the spread of this disease, and they decided","x":0.13360105767259767,"w":0.76987884521484373,"h":0.021750924163207341,"y":0.79613038478968201},{"t":"nutmeg held the cure. Everybody wanted nutmeg, and many were willing to spare no expense to","y":0.81418585581737468,"x":0.1336495852615521,"h":0.018887664741003896,"w":0.74092402140299474,"c":1},{"x":0.13362267631940805,"h":0.020849036945751909,"c":1,"y":0.82924896327937225,"t":"have it. Nutmeg bought for a few pennies in Indonesia could be sold for 68,000 times its original cost","w":0.78008509318033858},{"c":1,"x":0.13564643388873529,"y":0.84668009164310876,"w":0.75959711710611977,"t":"on the streets of London. The only problem was the short supply. And that's where the Dutch found","h":0.021144563654707516},{"h":0.019302716384366425,"w":0.13667067209879558,"y":0.86581557023691968,"t":"their opportunity.","c":1,"x":0.13535263148998505},{"x":0.13580246924831538,"y":0.92005813935786906,"c":1,"w":0.024691357612609849,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"16"}],"h":3395}